.SH "NAME"
nvme-tls-key \- Manage NVMe TLS PSKs (deprecated)
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.sp
.nf
\fInvme\fR [<global\-options>] \fItls\-key\fR [\-\-keyring=<name> | \-k <name>]
                        [\-\-keytype=<type> | \-t <type>]
                        [\-\-keyfile=<file> | \-f <file>]
                        [\-\-import | \-i] [\-\-export | \-e]
                        [\-\-revoke=<description> | \-r <description>]
.fi
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.sp
Deprecated command kept for scripts written against nvme\-cli versions older than 3\&.0\&. Exactly one of \fI\-\-import\fR, \fI\-\-export\fR, or \fI\-\-revoke\fR must be given; based on which mode is selected, this alias translates the command into the equivalent new \fIkeys\fR plugin subcommand and forwards to it:
.sp
.RS 4
.ie n \{\
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\c
.\}
.el \{\
.sp -1
.IP \(bu 2.3
.\}
\fI\-\-import\fR
translates to
\fBnvme-keys-import\fR(1), forwarding
\fI\-\-keyring\fR
and
\fI\-\-keyfile\fR\&.
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
.ie n \{\
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\c
.\}
.el \{\
.sp -1
.IP \(bu 2.3
.\}
\fI\-\-export\fR
translates to
\fBnvme-keys-export\fR(1), forwarding
\fI\-\-keyring\fR
and
\fI\-\-keyfile\fR\&.
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
.ie n \{\
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\c
.\}
.el \{\
.sp -1
.IP \(bu 2.3
.\}
\fI\-\-revoke=<description>\fR
translates to
\fBnvme-keys-revoke\fR(1), forwarding
\fI\-\-keyring\fR
and
\fI\-\-keytype\fR, with
\fI<description>\fR
passed as
\fI\-\-identity\fR\&.
.RE
.sp
Only the options relevant to the selected mode are meaningful; e\&.g\&. \fI\-\-keytype\fR has no effect with \fI\-\-import\fR or \fI\-\-export\fR since the new \fIimport\fR/\fIexport\fR subcommands no longer take a key type\&. This command does not derive or insert a TLS PSK from a configured PSK \(em use \fBnvme-keys-gen-tls-psk\fR(1) or \fBnvme-keys-insert-tls-psk\fR(1) for that\&.
.sp
New scripts should call \fInvme keys import\fR, \fInvme keys export\fR, or \fInvme keys revoke\fR directly instead\&. This alias prints a deprecation warning on stderr and may be removed in a future release\&.
.SH "OPTIONS"
.PP
\-k <name>, \-\-keyring=<name>
.RS 4
Name of the keyring to import into, export from, or revoke from\&. Default is
\fI\&.nvme\fR\&.
.RE
.PP
\-t <type>, \-\-keytype=<type>
.RS 4
Type of the key to revoke\&. Only used with
\fI\-\-revoke\fR\&. Default is
\fIpsk\fR\&.
.RE
.PP
\-f <file>, \-\-keyfile=<file>
.RS 4
File to read the keys from (\fI\-\-import\fR) or write the keys to (\fI\-\-export\fR) instead of stdin/stdout\&.
.RE
.PP
\-i, \-\-import
.RS 4
Import keys in bulk; see
\fBnvme-keys-import\fR(1)\&.
.RE
.PP
\-e, \-\-export
.RS 4
Export all keys from the keyring; see
\fBnvme-keys-export\fR(1)\&.
.RE
.PP
\-r <description>, \-\-revoke=<description>
.RS 4
Revoke the key stored under
\fI<description>\fR
from the keyring; see
\fBnvme-keys-revoke\fR(1)\&.
.RE
.SH "GLOBAL OPTIONS"
.sp
The following options are defined at the top\-level nvme command and are available to this subcommand:
.PP
\-\-dry\-run
.RS 4
Print the command that would be executed, but do not actually execute it\&.
.RE
.PP
\-\-no\-ioctl\-probing
.RS 4
Disable probing for 64\-bit IOCTL support\&.
.RE
.PP
\-\-no\-retries
.RS 4
Disable retry logic on transient errors\&.
.RE
.PP
\-o <fmt>, \-\-output\-format=<fmt>
.RS 4
Set the reporting format to
\fInormal\fR,
\fItabular, \*(Aqjson\fR, or
\fIbinary\fR\&. Only one output format may be used at a time\&.
.RE
.PP
\-\-output\-format\-version=<version>
.RS 4
Select the output format version\&. Version
\fI1\fR
uses the original field naming, while version
\fI2\fR
(default) provides more consistent and script\-friendly field names\&.
.RE
.PP
\-\-timeout=<ms>
.RS 4
Set the timeout for the command in milliseconds\&.
.RE
.PP
\-v, \-\-verbose
.RS 4
Increase the level of detail in the output\&. May be specified multiple times to further increase verbosity\&.
.RE
.sp
These options can also be set as machine\-wide defaults in nvme\-cli\&.conf(5)\&. A command\-line flag always overrides the file\&.
.SH "EXAMPLES"
